cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Architectures for Adaptive Filters for Image Denoising"
abstract: >-
  FPGA architectures for the six LMS adaptive-filter scenarios of image denoising (adaptive notch,
  bias canceller, canceller without a reference, self-tuning blind-spot predictor, adaptive line
  enhancer and reference-sensor canceller). The LMS loop is analysed from its iteration bound;
  six engines (serial, folded, direct-form and systolic delayed LMS, row-block LMS and distributed
  arithmetic) are derived, with the stability conditions of delayed and block LMS on images, a
  stall-free fixed-point weight accumulator, streaming front ends with reflected borders, and
  Verilog RTL that reproduces bit-accurate models word for word. Yosys resource counts and six
  application examples complete it.
